Copyright (c) 2026 NetNet Capital Management

An original game. No names, characters, maps, models, sounds or code from
any other game or franchise.

Art and sound
- Models come from the per-style asset library
  (@netnetcapital/asset-library): CC0 1.0 models by Quaternius (via Poly
  Pizza: the climbers and the coin) and Kenney (Nature Kit: trees, rocks,
  bushes), each pack listed with its
  source URL and licence verification in that package's NOTICE and
  manifest/packs.json. The files are fetched and built, never committed
  here; the build copies only the models this game uses.
- Blocks, ledges, thorns, springs, flags and the fallback climber
  (client/scene.ts) are generated from three.js primitives; all textures
  are drawn on a canvas at load. Sounds are the library's CC0 samples with
  WebAudio-synthesized fallbacks (client/audio.ts).

Dependencies (unmodified, via npm)
- three.js 0.186.1 (https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js), MIT.
- @netnetcapital/engine and @netnetcapital/engine-sim (this repository);
  see their NOTICE files (bitECS MPL-2.0, Rapier Apache-2.0, Colyseus MIT,
  zod MIT).

Patterns (ideas only)
- The platformer genre's general mechanics (run, jump, checkpoints, coins,
  springs, moving platforms, a flag at the end, racing to it). Mechanics,
  not expression; no level, character or text was copied from any game.
- Jump feel (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, apex hang,
  fall gravity, corner correction) as described in public game-feel talks
  and articles (e.g. "Math for Game Programmers: Building a Better Jump",
  GDC 2016; Maddy Thorson's public notes on Celeste's forgiveness
  mechanics). Implemented from scratch in engine-sim src/platform.ts.
